ORIGIN STORIES — Children's Educational Story App

================================================================================

For Kinsley (ages 4-12). AI-powered origin story generator.

Languages: English, Spanish, French, German, Portuguese, Japanese, Chinese.

================================================================================

APP OVERVIEW

================================================================================

User picks a topic (animals, science, food, nature, history, inventions),

selects a reading level (4-6 / 7-9 / 10-12), and the app generates a

multi-page illustrated story explaining the origin of that topic.

Features:

- Procedurally generated SVG illustrations (deterministic from seed)

- Multi-language support (7 languages)

- Bookshelf for saving stories

- Vocabulary section with new words

- Follow-up question feature

- Favorite system

================================================================================

TOPIC CATEGORIES

================================================================================

Animals: Butterflies, Dolphins, Dinosaurs, Fireflies, Penguins, Octopuses

Science: Rainbows, Stars, Magnets, Volcanoes, Gravity, Snowflakes

Food: Chocolate, Pizza, Ice Cream, Popcorn, Bread, Honey

Nature: The Moon, Waterfalls, Mountains, Coral Reefs, Forests, Caves

History: Pyramids, Castles, The Alphabet, Maps, Clocks, Music

Inventions: Bicycles, Telescopes, Hot Air Balloons, Crayons, Robots, Books

================================================================================

READING LEVEL GUIDES

================================================================================

Ages 4-6: Very simple words, short sentences (max 10 words), warm gentle tone,

sense of wonder. 50-70 words per section.

Ages 7-9: Accessible vocabulary with some interesting new words, moderate

sentences, adventurous tone. 90-120 words per section.

Ages 10-12: Rich vocabulary, varied sentences, deeper themes, fascinating

details. 130-180 words per section.

================================================================================

STORY STRUCTURE

================================================================================

Each generated story contains:

1. Opening page (sets the scene with wonder)

2. Chapter 1 — advance the narrative with real facts woven in

3. Chapter 2 — continue

4. Chapter 3 — continue

5. Conclusion — reveal how the topic became what it is, end with wonder

6. Vocabulary page — 3 new words with definitions

Each page has an SVG illustration generated from keyword analysis of the text.

================================================================================

ILLUSTRATION ENGINE

================================================================================

Procedural SVG — deterministic from seed + description keywords.

Sky palettes: day, dawn, sunset, night, misty, purple, cloudy.

Ground types: grass, sandy/desert, water/ocean, deep forest, earth/mountain, snow.

Elements detected from text: sun, moon, stars, mountains, water, trees, flowers,

snow, clouds, fire, food, books, buildings, inventions, animals, magic.

